    1. Pick grid 20x20, bg=0, fill=1, marker=2
    2. Choose N=3-4 rectangles with random heights/widths in [3,18]
    3. Place rectangles on grid with no overlap and min gap >= 2; allow edge-touching but keep g[0,0]=bg
    4. For each rectangle, choose a marker count = randint(2, ceil(0.25*area)), ensuring >= 1
    5. Adjust counts so exactly one rectangle has strictly the largest marker count (the winner); ensure winner has at least 2 more markers than runner-up
    6. For each rectangle, scatter its marker pixels randomly within the rectangle, filling rest with fill color
    7. Verify total marker count < total fill count (marker is the rarer color)
